1028 0 obj
<<
/ActualText (ACER - Australian Council for Educational Research\(Senior Frontend Developer - Contracted \n\nIn January, I was contracted to help build out the new front-end of the ACER Preschool Outcomes Measures tool, an educational platform used by teachers to assess children in the classroom. The project involved a complete redesign, and I was part of a small design, UX, and development team. The app was built using Svelte with Web Components, and we developed primarily inside a Storybook environment. This allowed us to build out the components, pages, and all the UI states while the backend team built out the APIs. There was high priority placed on making the app accessible to schools in remote communities where internet speeds are spotty, so we focused on lean bundle sizes with Vite as our bundler, and on selectively generating static pages where possible. )
