/ActualText (ABC\(Senior Frontend Developer - Full-time\n\nAs a member of the ABC News Digital team I refactored the abc.net.au/news page layout. The mobile layout had a different ordering of components compared to the desktop version, and there were duplicate components being rendered to achieve this complex ordering. I introduced CSS Grid, which allowed us to position a single component in different \030slots\031 of a grid for different breakpoints. This optimisation reduced the amount of code and bundle size, resulting in a significantly smoother and more responsive experience. I also implemented dark mode styles for the 2022 national election pages across both web and mobile app platforms. Additionally, I had the notable opportunity to work on the front-page coverage of Queen Elizabeth II's passing. The tech stack used was React/Next.JS, Storybook and GraphQL.)
/K [5]
/S /Span
